cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "agrilok: a source-cited AI study platform for Nepal's Loksewa agriculture exams"
message: "If you use this project or its approach in your work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ganesh
    family-names: Chaudhary
    email: ganeshchaudhary4400@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ganesh-786/agrilok"
abstract: >-
  agrilok is a free, open-source retrieval-augmented study platform for the
  Nepal Public Service Commission agriculture service examinations at Level 4
  (Junior Technical Assistant) and Level 7 (Officer). It crawls whitelisted
  official federal and provincial sources, extracts and human-reviews the
  material, and generates study answers strictly from retrieved text so that
  every answer carries a resolvable citation back to the originating government
  document. The design targets sustained free operation on free-tier
  infrastructure through cache-first serving, and low-bandwidth rural delivery
  through a progressive web app.
keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - education
  - nepal
  - loksewa
  - agriculture
  - public-service-commission
  - nepali-nlp
  - low-resource-languages
